/P 1206 0 R
/E (A regression tree follows the same steps as a classification tree, but with a few key differences. Instead of calculating entropy, we calculate the squared error, which measures how far the predicted values are from the actual values. And instead of using the Information Gain to choose the best split, we look at the sum of squared errors \(SSE\). The split that gives us the lowest SSE is chosen as the next split in the tree.)
